1
00:00:06,256 --> 00:00:08,216
M DO G AN

2
00:00:09,759 --> 00:00:12,344
Man, we don't know who the client is,
I swear.

3
00:00:12,345 --> 00:00:14,346
- You gotta believe us!
- Shut up!

4
00:00:14,347 --> 00:00:16,515
Ow! What the hell? I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

5
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:18,851
- I won't do it again, I promise!
- I'll never do anything illegal again.

6
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:20,352
I'll be a good boy, I swear to you!

7
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,979
A little late for that, don't you think?

8
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,147
I'm telling you the truth.

9
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:26,358
Once we get paid,
we just write comments online, that's all.

10
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:29,194
Just trendy shit.
It's just to bring in traffic.

11
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:31,364
That's called manipulating the public,
you idiot.

12
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:34,700
It explains why we've got a cyber unit
all of a sudden.

13
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:36,286
Hey. What's your name?

14
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:38,371
You listening? What's your name?

15
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,793
This is a <i>nagari</i>.

16
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:46,837
Where did you pick up that phrase?

17
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:49,340
Oh, it came up
on the Korean shows I watch.

18
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:53,303
Uh, on your feet.

19
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:57,514
- Hello, ma'am.
- Hello, ma'am.

20
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:58,640
Hi.

21
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:01,186
You fuckers and your damn cigarettes.

22
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:07,941
Why are you wasting your time
on some internet trolls

23
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:09,443
instead of a serial killer?

24
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:10,986
Whose decision was this?

25
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:12,113
I apologize.

26
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:14,531
Quiet. Don't move.

27
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:18,702
How about you go apologize to your parents
for being such a colossal moron?

28
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:22,539
Is there anything in between those ears
at all, you absolute stupid idiot?

29
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:24,958
God, why are you even alive?
Breathing the same oxygen as us.

30
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,543
This is really
the head of the investigation unit?

31
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:27,921
- Yes, she is.
- Oh.

32
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:33,843
Oh. Hey, the Japanese guy,
you're here too?

33
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:36,846
Uh, yeah. Hi.

34
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:39,682
Lovely to meet you, sir.

35
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:42,226
Oh, I'm the head
of the Mobile Investigation Unit.

36
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:44,645
Oh. It's nice to meet you.

37
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:48,440
I must apologize
for you having to deal with these morons.

38
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:51,236
And after coming all this way
to our country, too.

39
00:01:53,571 --> 00:01:55,948
- Say something, Inose.
- Ah, it's all right.

40
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,407
Oh, great. I'm glad.

41
00:01:57,408 --> 00:02:00,077
In any case, let your bosses know

42
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:03,330
everything is going just fine over here.

43
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:06,416
Korean detectives
are excellent at what they do.

44
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:08,711
Oh. Yeah, I absolutely will.

45
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,217
- Yeah.
- Jesus, this is mortifying.

46
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:17,637
What was that? What just happened?

47
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:21,015
If I have to hear about
any more of your failures...

48
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:24,059
I'll disband this force.

49
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,395
Yes, ma'am!

50
00:02:27,188 --> 00:02:28,898
Useless sons of bitches.

51
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:32,694
Ma'am...

52
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:43,163
Come on. Let's go. I need a smoke.

53
00:02:43,746 --> 00:02:45,622
- You in?
- For sure. I need some air.

54
00:02:45,623 --> 00:02:48,501
Something is off with that kid.

55
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:52,337
Oh, yeah. Why?

56
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:54,840
Come on. Let's go. Everyone in, faster.
Move it. Let's go!

57
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:55,925
Hey, you, come here.

58
00:02:56,676 --> 00:02:59,011
We need to have a chat. Just a second.

59
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,095
Move it! Get your butts in there.

60
00:03:00,096 --> 00:03:01,389
- Over here.
- But why?

61
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:03,599
So...

62
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,602
You have no idea what prison is like,
do you?

63
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:07,812
Come on. Right here.

64
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:10,481
Wh-What do you want with me?

65
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:14,151
You... know something.

66
00:03:14,152 --> 00:03:15,235
What?

67
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:17,738
If you cooperate,
we'll put in a good word.

68
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:19,949
You'll just go to juvenile detention
instead of prison.

69
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:23,952
Oh, really?

70
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:26,706
- Really.
- But that'll depend on what you tell us.

71
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:29,459
Okay?

72
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:34,714
Okay, prison, then.

73
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:38,259
- No, no, no, wait!
- Hmm?

74
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:40,887
- That post.
- Yes?

75
00:03:45,266 --> 00:03:48,895
I looked at the account
of the guy who hired us to write it.

76
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:55,067
I know the post was just
about the Imjin War and stuff, but...

77
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:56,902
THE HISTORY OF EMIRI,
THE UNSUNG HERO OF THE IMJIN WAR

78
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:57,987
<i>It was kinda weird.</i>

79
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:01,699
"The Imjin War."

80
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:04,369
This a prank or what?

81
00:04:05,536 --> 00:04:09,082
<i>The whole thing just seemed weird,
so I looked at the guy's profile.</i>

82
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:12,501
REQUESTING A FORUM POST @EMI

83
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:13,670
"Emi"?

84
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:15,463
Hmm.

85
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:19,467
THIS ACCOUNT HAS BEEN DELETED

86
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,010
I do remember it said "Emi".

87
00:04:22,011 --> 00:04:24,221
Uh, E-M-I! That's what's it said.

88
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:26,724
Though, I'm pretty sure
the account is deleted now.

89
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:35,566
The person who asked you to post
about Emiri, his name was just, uh... hmm...

90
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:38,444
Emi, is that it?

91
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,822
Uh, yeah.

92
00:04:41,572 --> 00:04:43,407
My, you've been a real big help,
haven't you?

93
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:45,325
Kiss that reduced sentence goodbye.

94
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:47,494
- Get him on the bus.
- All right. Let's go.

95
00:04:47,495 --> 00:04:50,038
- Off you go.
- Wait, go where? What?

96
00:04:50,039 --> 00:04:51,581
- I said let's go. Come on, you heard.
- Wait.

97
00:04:51,582 --> 00:04:52,791
- But you said you'd help me!
- Easy now.

98
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:54,711
- Just go.
- Hey! Stop! No! No, please!

99
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,587
- Shut your mouth. Get in, now.
- You're hurting me!

100
00:04:57,588 --> 00:04:59,007
YANGHWA SUPERMARKET

101
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:06,139
Have a good night.

102
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:32,290
What, you're not gonna share?

103
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:34,375
How mean.

104
00:05:38,546 --> 00:05:41,590
I think it's safe to say,
you don't have any friends, huh?

105
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:42,675
So?

106
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:45,428
I see.

107
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:50,558
Golden boy of the police academy
who doesn't care about anybody.

108
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:55,188
You still live with your mom, don't you?

109
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,068
The murderer...

110
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:06,032
is more clever than I thought.

111
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:10,453
He probably knows
quite a lot about us, too.

112
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:15,291
He wanted to see
if we'd take the bait or not.

113
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:18,002
But he's gonna be far more careful now.

114
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,801
Yes?

115
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:27,136
What?

116
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:29,180
The trunk of a car?

117
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:31,182
I'll be right there.

118
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:33,684
Understood.

119
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:41,733
They just found a woman
who was kidnapped from Seoul.

120
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:43,111
She escaped in Gunsan.

121
00:06:45,571 --> 00:06:46,739
Remember what the Chinese guy said?

122
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:51,786
It seems they found a tiger
at the killer's house.

123
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:49,135
THE BLUE ROAD

124
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:54,139
THE CATHOLIC UNIVERSITY OF KOREA
UIJEONGBU ST. MARY'S HOSPITAL

125
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:57,560
The escaped victim's testimony
is similar to that of our current case.

126
00:07:58,644 --> 00:08:01,397
But how was she even able to escape
if she was unconscious?

127
00:08:01,981 --> 00:08:03,565
The patient, Ms. Lee Hyeon-seo,

128
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:06,693
had a tracheostomy for a tumor
she had in her larynx as a child.

129
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:09,780
'Cause of that, she's been on painkillers
for pretty much her entire life.

130
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:12,199
And because of her acclimation to them,

131
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:14,202
when the perpetrator
administered his drugs...

132
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:16,871
She managed to fight
against their effects.

133
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,540
So that's how she was able to escape?

134
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:23,920
Yep. It's also why she became an addict.

135
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:29,842
She also has a congenital heart defect,
so try not to rattle her.

136
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:31,928
She needs peace and quiet.

137
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:43,314
So the murderer used Speed K to lure in
a new victim, just like they did before.

138
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:45,691
Well, let's meet her.

139
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,324
Excuse me, miss?

140
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:55,825
We're detectives with the Seoul police.

141
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:57,161
Can we ask you a...

142
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,468
That man.

143
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:16,264
I wanna put him in jail.

144
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:21,185
I wasn't able to
get a good look at his face.

145
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:27,608
Please find him, officers.

146
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:45,835
I promise.

147
00:09:47,044 --> 00:09:48,629
We'll find this guy.

148
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,301
But for us to do that, we need your help.

149
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:58,264
This might seem a little strange.

150
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:03,227
Uh, Inose, care to fill me in please?

151
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:06,980
Yes, ma'am.

152
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:11,152
It's a method that the FBI uses during
the early stages of their investigations.

153
00:10:11,777 --> 00:10:15,698
And, uh, Inose claims
he did it when he was in the States.

154
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:17,824
During training and also in the field.

155
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:19,910
<i>Hang on. Isn't she from an orphanage?</i>

156
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:21,536
<i>She has no guardian, right?</i>

157
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:23,997
<i>Are you gonna take responsibility?
Huh? Are you?</i>

158
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:26,500
Chief Gu messed up already.
Just let us try this.

159
00:10:28,252 --> 00:10:29,462
I'll take responsibility.

160
00:10:30,087 --> 00:10:31,964
<i>Listen...</i>

161
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:41,098
Right, let's give this a shot.

162
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:42,933
Gotta pull out all the stops.

163
00:10:53,235 --> 00:10:56,322
I've got a daughter. She liked this.

164
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:03,788
Hmm?

165
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:10,252
Hmm.

166
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,298
Hmm.

167
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:18,886
Here. Take it.

168
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:34,443
Buy yourself some ice cream.

169
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:42,284
Now, try to relax.

170
00:11:56,882 --> 00:11:58,843
I'm now going to count to ten.

171
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:02,471
One.

172
00:12:03,472 --> 00:12:04,682
Two.

173
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:06,726
Three.

174
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:09,270
Four.

175
00:12:11,063 --> 00:12:12,064
Five.

176
00:12:14,066 --> 00:12:15,067
Six.

177
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:18,154
Seven.

178
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,198
Eight.

179
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:29,123
<i>It's dark.</i>

180
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,336
<i>It's pitch black.</i>

181
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:39,842
<i>I can hear someone playing a piano.</i>

182
00:12:43,304 --> 00:12:45,014
<i>It's an old house.</i>

183
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,895
<i>Or at least, it looks like an old house.</i>

184
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:56,942
<i>There's a tiger.</i>

185
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:04,575
<i>Or, it's a tiger-shaped...</i>

186
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:12,416
<i>device.</i>

187
00:13:18,255 --> 00:13:19,924
<i>He's coming closer.</i>

188
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:29,266
<i>I'm pretending to be asleep.</i>

189
00:13:34,814 --> 00:13:38,442
<i>And then, once his guard is down...</i>

190
00:14:10,766 --> 00:14:11,934
I'm scared.

191
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:16,730
He's...

192
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,401
a monster.

193
00:14:25,072 --> 00:14:26,407
I'm begging you.

194
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:32,121
If you don't catch him,
he'll hunt me down.

195
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:34,665
Please find him.

196
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:37,501
We will.

197
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:42,256
GUNSAN

198
00:14:44,508 --> 00:14:46,885
The victim was kidnapped in Seoul.

199
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:50,597
He stuffed her into a large vehicle
and drove all the way to Gunsan.

200
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:53,933
Look for any old houses, and vehicles
that could have been modified.

201
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:57,687
And make sure to check every
Japanese resident in Gunsan. Understood?

202
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:58,771
Yes, sir!

203
00:14:58,772 --> 00:15:00,189
Wow, this is cramped.

204
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:01,399
Come on, man, we gotta move!

205
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,525
Yes, sir.

206
00:15:02,526 --> 00:15:04,652
I told you not to put this in the back!

207
00:15:04,653 --> 00:15:07,572
Come on! How many times I gotta say it?

208
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:08,657
Uh...

209
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:12,827
So this bus is gonna act
as our main operations base?

210
00:15:12,828 --> 00:15:14,371
That's Korea for you.

211
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,165
That right?

212
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:20,711
Hey, Inspector Kim,
what's your buddy's problem, huh?

213
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:23,756
Oh, uh...

214
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:27,634
He's just impressed with Korea's

215
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:30,763
knack for undercover operations
and surveillance abilities.

216
00:15:32,681 --> 00:15:33,766
It's cool, right?

217
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:38,269
So this guy seems really scary,
but he's a big old softy, isn't he?

218
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:40,104
Hey, listen up, everyone!

219
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,731
Don't fucking screw this up this time!

220
00:15:41,732 --> 00:15:43,816
- Yes, sir!
- Let's go! Move it!

221
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:47,112
Remember, this is undercover!
Don't blow our cover to the Gunsan cops!

222
00:15:48,155 --> 00:15:49,698
This is our operations base, I guess.

223
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:51,200
Huh?

224
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:53,786
Uh...

225
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:57,038
I'm sure you probably noticed already,

226
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,791
but Gunsan is on the small side.

227
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:02,878
He'll find out fast.

228
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:04,588
What?

229
00:16:07,549 --> 00:16:10,510
That we've created
a special investigations force

230
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:12,220
and are closing in on him.

231
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:13,305
The killer.

232
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:20,186
After Lee Hyeon-seo escaped,
she ran for a full hour.

233
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:23,690
That means she was held somewhere
within this five-kilometer radius.

234
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:27,111
A place that has enough room
for an oversized vehicle, like a van.

235
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:30,446
The building also
has to have a large basement.

236
00:16:30,447 --> 00:16:31,657
That's what we should look for.

237
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:36,370
Well, Chief Gu should
be able to handle that with his guys.

238
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:43,168
As for us, let's put our minds together.

239
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:50,759
So both Lee Hyeon-seo
and the Chinese guy mentioned a tiger.

240
00:16:53,762 --> 00:16:56,181
A large device
designed to look like a tiger.

241
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:00,811
Could it be some kind of torture device?

242
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:05,106
TORTURE DEVICE DESIGNED
TO BREAK BONES AND JOINTS

243
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:06,233
Definitely not that one.

244
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:11,447
Right. A device like that

245
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:15,200
would crush the bones entirely,
not just twist them around.

246
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:19,454
So you fasten their limbs,
and then break them

247
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:22,499
by turning the handle
until they finally snap?

248
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:25,461
More like a crack.

249
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:28,005
Cracking, cracking.

250
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:31,091
<i>Crack.</i>

251
00:17:33,677 --> 00:17:37,848
<i>The sound of bones breaking.</i>

252
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:41,477
<i>The sound of...</i>

253
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:43,771
Huh...

254
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:47,566
what if it's not
a torture device after all?

255
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:54,198
So, the sound of cracking and screaming...

256
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:59,161
And Lee Hyeon-seo
heard the sound of a piano.

257
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:06,126
<i>He does it to get the sounds?</i>

258
00:18:09,797 --> 00:18:11,840
What if he's not interested in torture?

259
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:15,135
Not interested in torture.

260
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,347
Twisting their body.

261
00:18:19,556 --> 00:18:21,225
He makes music with it?

262
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:23,102
Yeah.

263
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:29,691
TIGER INSTRUMENT

264
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:33,403
COMMUNITY ART
THE TIGER OF THE ANCESTRAL MOUNTAIN

265
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:35,405
- You seeing that?
- Yeah.

266
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:39,284
The Tiger of the Ancestral Mountain.

267
00:18:42,412 --> 00:18:44,247
ALL THE SOUNDS IN THE WORLD

268
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:47,834
"The Tiger of the Ancestral Mountain
symbolizes the Tiger of Joseon,

269
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:50,419
an art piece made
during the Japanese colonial era."

270
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,754
"The piece turns the great tiger

271
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:53,757
that terrorized Korea
into a musical instrument."

272
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:56,926
"When the instrument is played,

273
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:59,554
one hears the sound of bones breaking
and tendons snapping."

274
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:01,723
"However, we don't know
how the instrument operates."

275
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:07,855
@EMI'S PROFILE

276
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:12,401
"E-M-I."

277
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:16,405
I do remember it said "Emi".
Uh, E-M-I! That's what's it said.

278
00:19:16,905 --> 00:19:18,447
EMI SHUNSUKE EXHIBITION CREATOR,
PIANIST, SOUND ARTIST

279
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:19,741
"Emi Shunsuke."

280
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:21,410
Japanese?

281
00:19:24,913 --> 00:19:26,289
GUNSAN FOREIGN RESIDENT REGISTRY

282
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,374
Emi.

283
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,001
Could it maybe be a stage name?

284
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,794
Emi Shunsuke.

285
00:19:31,795 --> 00:19:33,254
Emi, Emi.

286
00:19:33,255 --> 00:19:36,508
Emi Shunsuke,
address is 35-47 Buksan-dong.

287
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:38,468
Here, Buksan-dong.

288
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:40,512
Within the five-kilometer radius.

289
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:42,139
Right here.

290
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:53,024
Uh, hello, Chief. Sorry for the message,
but we're moving fast.

291
00:19:53,025 --> 00:19:54,108
Call us back ASAP.

292
00:19:54,109 --> 00:19:55,693
Hey. Hey! Detective Kim!

293
00:19:55,694 --> 00:19:58,070
There's Emi Shunsuke
and Emi from Shogun Emiri.

294
00:19:58,071 --> 00:19:59,280
They sound alike.

295
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:00,782
Emi isn't a common name in Japan.

296
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:04,369
Listen, if I don't answer your call later,

297
00:20:05,412 --> 00:20:07,664
uh, please track both our locations.

298
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:31,104
Are we already too late?

299
00:20:39,154 --> 00:20:40,864
Wait. I've seen this before.

300
00:20:44,159 --> 00:20:46,119
Don't.

301
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:49,248
Look at that.

302
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,752
Aw, come on!

303
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:57,964
Who the hell thought of
parking their bus like this here? Huh?

304
00:20:57,965 --> 00:21:00,050
I'm gonna get it towed!

305
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:02,260
This your bus?

306
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:04,471
- You can't park here! Move it!
- We're police, from Seoul.

307
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:06,848
- You're police?
- Yes.

308
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:09,601
Does anybody named
Emi Shunsuke live around here?

309
00:21:12,521 --> 00:21:14,730
Shunsuke, you mean, the artist?

310
00:21:14,731 --> 00:21:16,274
- He's an artist?
- Yes.

311
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:18,484
- Can you tell me where he is?
- Hello, there.

312
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:20,820
Inose Hiroshi, miss.

313
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:22,447
I'm here from Japan.

314
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:26,827
- Oh, you're Japanese too?
- Yes.

315
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:31,665
Ah, that Emi Shunsuke, I'm an
old friend of his from his hometown.

316
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:34,375
- You're from his hometown?
- Yeah.

317
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:37,879
I was really just hoping
to see an old friend.

318
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:40,924
This Korean police officer
is lending a hand.

319
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:44,844
Oh. Is... Is that so?

320
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,096
Oh, wow.

321
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:50,559
You guys have come a long way. Well, okay.

322
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:57,482
What?

323
00:21:59,609 --> 00:22:00,610
What is it?

324
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:05,114
I'm sorry.
You've traveled so far in this heat.

325
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:07,074
I wish I had
something better to serve you.

326
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:09,202
Ah, forgive me.

327
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:12,455
- Have a slice of this watermelon.
- Thank you.

328
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:13,914
And some tea.

329
00:22:13,915 --> 00:22:15,000
You two are close?

330
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:19,211
Well, he tends to stay rather quiet,
you know.

331
00:22:19,212 --> 00:22:23,008
He's a very kind person,
but not very outgoing.

332
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:27,303
Whenever he has to travel
and expects to be away for a while,

333
00:22:27,304 --> 00:22:29,513
I'm the one who gets his mail and whatnot.

334
00:22:29,514 --> 00:22:30,766
You find he travels a lot?

335
00:22:32,601 --> 00:22:35,020
Uh. Well, sometimes.

336
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:39,315
He travels to go put on shows,
show off his art. That sort of thing.

337
00:22:39,316 --> 00:22:41,109
Here, here. Let me pour you a drink.

338
00:22:46,114 --> 00:22:47,908
Has Shunsuke...

339
00:22:50,410 --> 00:22:52,244
Has he lived here very long?

340
00:22:52,245 --> 00:22:54,288
I'm not really sure.

341
00:22:54,289 --> 00:22:57,583
He's been here since well before
I moved into the neighborhood,

342
00:22:57,584 --> 00:22:59,710
so I imagine
he's been here for quite a while.

343
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:01,420
He's very liked around here, too.

344
00:23:01,421 --> 00:23:04,132
He does a lot of volunteer work
around the community.

345
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:06,217
Oh! You know what?

346
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:09,845
He mentioned that his house
has been passed down for generations.

347
00:23:09,846 --> 00:23:10,931
Over centuries.

348
00:23:13,016 --> 00:23:15,935
As you can see,
this house is perfect for him,

349
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:18,187
since he needs to work in peace and quiet

350
00:23:18,188 --> 00:23:20,857
to be able to create his art
without distractions.

351
00:23:21,983 --> 00:23:26,237
In fact, the way I see it,
it's a perfect area for an artist.

352
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:29,490
You need solitude for lightning to strike.

353
00:23:29,491 --> 00:23:33,787
I became a pretty big fan of his
after living next door for so long.

354
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:39,167
Oh, who could be calling me now?
Who could this be?

355
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:43,088
Yes, hello?

356
00:23:43,588 --> 00:23:45,298
Oh, it's you, Mr. Emi!

357
00:23:46,508 --> 00:23:48,050
How did your rehearsal go?

358
00:23:48,051 --> 00:23:49,553
Oh. Oh.

359
00:23:50,345 --> 00:23:53,597
You said two days? Oh, of course.
Don't worry about it!

360
00:23:53,598 --> 00:23:56,810
I can take care of your garden.
No worries.

361
00:23:58,145 --> 00:23:59,146
What?

362
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:01,689
How did you know?

363
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:03,775
Sure.

364
00:24:05,944 --> 00:24:07,154
It's for you.

365
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:10,906
What?

366
00:24:10,907 --> 00:24:12,909
Mr. Emi wants to talk to you.

367
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:16,413
- Seriously?
- Yes. Hurry up. He's waiting.

368
00:24:17,247 --> 00:24:18,582
Come on! Take the phone!

369
00:24:22,544 --> 00:24:23,878
Yes, can I help you?

370
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:25,505
<i>So you're a detective, right?</i>

371
00:24:30,135 --> 00:24:32,429
<i>Can you explain why you're looking for me?</i>

372
00:24:33,263 --> 00:24:34,263
<i>Hmm.</i>

373
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:37,267
<i>Look, my Korean is a little rough, but...</i>

374
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:41,021
<i>Am I the culprit?</i>

375
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:43,190
<i>Could I be the culprit?</i>

376
00:24:50,530 --> 00:24:52,491
<i>I'm here at the police station.</i>

377
00:25:04,878 --> 00:25:08,214
It's my pleasure, officers.
Thank you for your hard work.

378
00:25:08,215 --> 00:25:09,673
...brought us pastries
to thank us for our hard work.

379
00:25:09,674 --> 00:25:11,175
- Please, enjoy.
- Thank you!

380
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:12,510
- You know, he's a famous artist! Wow!
- Oh, hello.

381
00:25:12,511 --> 00:25:13,845
Can I help you two?

382
00:25:14,346 --> 00:25:17,890
Hey! Say thank you! Here, take one.
Yes, stuff your face.

383
00:25:17,891 --> 00:25:19,850
- Wow, thank you.
- Here, enjoy. You deserve it.

384
00:25:19,851 --> 00:25:21,560
Do they know Mr. Emi?

385
00:25:21,561 --> 00:25:22,978
Here, pass me one.

386
00:25:22,979 --> 00:25:25,564
Anyone who hasn't gotten a pastry,
come grab one.

387
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:27,859
We've got red bean buns, soboro buns.

388
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:33,782
Hello.

389
00:25:35,158 --> 00:25:36,535
Right.

390
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:42,874
Let's see.
Oh, uh, no, there's only one left.

391
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:54,761
It's nice to meet you.

392
00:26:03,853 --> 00:26:05,730
I'm Emi Shunsuke.

393
00:26:08,066 --> 00:26:10,694
Forgive me,
but you seem disappointed.

394
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:22,247
Whoa, whoa!

395
00:26:23,290 --> 00:26:24,290
What are you doing?

396
00:26:24,291 --> 00:26:25,375
Hey!

397
00:26:29,671 --> 00:26:31,005
Oh, my...

398
00:26:31,006 --> 00:26:32,674
Look at this.

399
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:34,717
It's like they've all moved in here.

400
00:26:34,718 --> 00:26:36,303
Nice little set-up.

401
00:26:36,845 --> 00:26:38,137
It's like they've made themselves
a whole office.

402
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:40,472
- They've made themselves quite cozy here.
- Oh, my God. What the hell?

403
00:26:40,473 --> 00:26:41,724
It's like a secret hideout.

404
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:43,225
Who do these guys think they are?

405
00:26:43,226 --> 00:26:44,852
- What, are they undercover?
- Whoa.

406
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:45,936
This is bullshit.

407
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:48,606
Kim Seok, that asshole.

408
00:26:48,607 --> 00:26:50,733
You don't even
offer a joint investigation?

409
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:53,444
Are we a bunch of idiots to you?
Is that it? Huh?

410
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:54,528
Hey, don't twist it!

411
00:26:54,529 --> 00:26:57,364
We had no choice. The investigation
had to be kept on the down-low, okay?

412
00:26:57,365 --> 00:26:58,490
- You son of a...
- Knock it off.

413
00:26:58,491 --> 00:26:59,908
That's enough. Here, look.

414
00:26:59,909 --> 00:27:01,285
Oh, give me a fucking break!

415
00:27:01,286 --> 00:27:03,454
You bastards just ride on in
to someone else's jurisdiction?

416
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:05,414
That's an official order.
You can't just ignore it.

417
00:27:05,415 --> 00:27:07,959
- Come on, you son of a bitch.
- This is our turf.

418
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:12,339
INTERROGATION ROOM
GUNSAN POLICE STATION

419
00:27:13,048 --> 00:27:15,174
What you said over the phone earlier.

420
00:27:15,175 --> 00:27:16,760
What exactly did I say?

421
00:27:26,561 --> 00:27:27,937
Hello!

422
00:27:29,939 --> 00:27:31,608
Hey. Pay attention.

423
00:27:33,318 --> 00:27:35,904
Aren't you pretty young
to be a famous artist?

424
00:27:37,656 --> 00:27:38,657
You think so?

425
00:27:41,951 --> 00:27:43,952
Kinda funny that we're here, right?

426
00:27:43,953 --> 00:27:47,164
We're both Japanese, sitting across from
each other in a Korean police station.

427
00:27:47,165 --> 00:27:49,208
Why's that funny?

428
00:27:49,209 --> 00:27:52,670
The fact that we're both Japanese
is why I'm interrogating you.

429
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:55,547
Planning exhibitions,
piano performances, sound art.

430
00:27:55,548 --> 00:27:57,592
What kind of work do you do, exactly?

431
00:27:58,176 --> 00:28:01,387
I mean, I create art, obviously.

432
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:02,554
I focus on works of art

433
00:28:02,555 --> 00:28:06,226
that fuse together the senses of sight
and hearing into one experience.

434
00:28:07,143 --> 00:28:09,687
Come to my next show,
and you can see for yourself.

435
00:28:09,688 --> 00:28:12,356
This one is going to be
an interactive sound piece,

436
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,857
with a little bit of performance art too.

437
00:28:13,858 --> 00:28:16,736
The Tiger of the Ancestral Mountain.
You made that, didn't you?

438
00:28:18,071 --> 00:28:21,365
Says here, you often go back and forth
between Korea and Japan.

439
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:22,825
You and your tiger device.

440
00:28:22,826 --> 00:28:26,662
Ah, the tiger.
It's an exhibit and an instrument.

441
00:28:26,663 --> 00:28:27,746
It's one of a kind.

442
00:28:27,747 --> 00:28:30,040
It's not something
that can be defined as one thing.

443
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:32,292
The sounds that come out of it
are just magic.

444
00:28:32,293 --> 00:28:34,337
- It creates this unbelievable effect.
- So your art...

445
00:28:37,882 --> 00:28:39,759
It requires murder, is that it?

446
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:55,567
Detective, you have a...

447
00:28:57,819 --> 00:29:00,071
very nice vocal energy, I must say.

448
00:29:00,822 --> 00:29:01,948
Okay, and so what?

449
00:29:02,532 --> 00:29:06,452
Your vocal register might sit a little
higher than an average man of your age,

450
00:29:06,453 --> 00:29:09,496
but your energy creates
powerful sound waves,

451
00:29:09,497 --> 00:29:12,750
which activate the frequencies
that flow through our minds and bodies.

452
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:15,962
I barely graduated high school.
You're barking up the wrong tree.

453
00:29:16,755 --> 00:29:18,840
Your voice is so soothing.

454
00:29:19,424 --> 00:29:21,760
It's the kind
that inspires the human soul.

455
00:29:22,635 --> 00:29:24,387
It makes me want to play with it.

456
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:33,646
Awfully high and mighty
for a cold-blooded killer, huh?

457
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:40,153
What time is it?

458
00:29:52,457 --> 00:29:54,333
Takes some pretty big balls

459
00:29:54,334 --> 00:29:57,044
to come to the police station
with the murder vehicle.

460
00:29:57,045 --> 00:29:59,087
Hey, hey, don't touch it!
Get off! Back away!

461
00:29:59,088 --> 00:30:01,632
- Please, one fingerprint.
- Hey, hey!

462
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:03,218
How much longer we gotta wait?

463
00:30:03,843 --> 00:30:05,302
Can't we just bust it open?

464
00:30:05,303 --> 00:30:08,388
Don't be dumb.
You know we need a warrant first.

465
00:30:08,389 --> 00:30:10,682
- Just wait.
- Oh, for God's sake!

466
00:30:10,683 --> 00:30:13,519
This is bullshit!
What the hell are you doing? Huh?

467
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:15,729
What in the world
are you guys doing right there?

468
00:30:15,730 --> 00:30:17,272
Just hanging around
with a bunch of hammers?

469
00:30:17,273 --> 00:30:18,482
- The fuck?
- You son of a bitch.

470
00:30:18,483 --> 00:30:21,026
Whoa, whoa!
Everyone just calm down, calm down!

471
00:30:21,027 --> 00:30:23,111
Don't you dare touch that car.

472
00:30:23,112 --> 00:30:26,115
Not until we get probable cause
or a warrant, got it?

473
00:30:28,743 --> 00:30:29,744
Mmm, this is good.

474
00:30:35,917 --> 00:30:39,379
Man, this is good. Not gonna have any?

475
00:30:40,088 --> 00:30:42,507
I noticed that you came here
in a pretty big car.

476
00:30:43,007 --> 00:30:45,801
Well, yeah. I need that space
for my equipment and stuff.

477
00:30:45,802 --> 00:30:50,181
Oh, equipment, I see,
and kidnapping young women, right?

478
00:30:50,849 --> 00:30:54,184
And of course,
you need room for your tiger as well.

479
00:30:54,185 --> 00:30:56,396
How many people can you fit in that trunk?

480
00:30:58,106 --> 00:31:01,651
I guess if they're dead, you can
stuff more than if they were alive.

481
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:04,320
Especially if their limbs were broken.

482
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:07,907
How should I know?

483
00:31:08,616 --> 00:31:10,909
I've never stuffed anyone
in a trunk before.

484
00:31:10,910 --> 00:31:13,079
I live alone, no family or anything.

485
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:18,209
I was told your house was passed down over
generations, but weirdly, your parents...

486
00:31:18,835 --> 00:31:21,546
I couldn't find a single record
of them anywhere.

487
00:31:23,631 --> 00:31:26,467
What, did they disown you?
Cut you out of the will?

488
00:31:28,177 --> 00:31:30,179
Do your parents even know?

489
00:31:31,055 --> 00:31:33,057
That their son is a murderer?

490
00:31:35,935 --> 00:31:39,230
Do I really have to divulge
private information like that?

491
00:31:40,982 --> 00:31:41,983
Yes.

492
00:31:44,444 --> 00:31:45,945
Yes, you do.

493
00:31:46,529 --> 00:31:49,824
Excuse me.
I think your chair is a little wobbly.

494
00:31:57,248 --> 00:32:00,042
Your family witnessed some of your crimes,
is that it?

495
00:32:00,043 --> 00:32:03,670
Or is it that you tried to take them out?

496
00:32:03,671 --> 00:32:07,549
Oh, Detective.
You certainly have a vivid imagination.

497
00:32:07,550 --> 00:32:09,551
Oh, man.

498
00:32:09,552 --> 00:32:13,597
Oh, Detective. Detective.

499
00:32:13,598 --> 00:32:14,682
Yeah?

500
00:32:16,017 --> 00:32:18,895
Um, may I ask?

501
00:32:22,315 --> 00:32:23,775
What time is it?

502
00:32:27,487 --> 00:32:30,864
Oh, man. that hurt.

503
00:32:30,865 --> 00:32:32,366
Ouch, that really hurt.

504
00:32:32,367 --> 00:32:34,953
Oof, I'm gonna be sore tomorrow.

505
00:32:37,205 --> 00:32:38,455
No drug offenses.

506
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:40,332
He was on Jeju Island
when Park In-gyu died.

507
00:32:40,333 --> 00:32:42,376
No records of travel
when Miyashita Aki was killed.

508
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:43,503
He thought of everything.

509
00:32:44,087 --> 00:32:46,713
So, does that mean
we don't get a search warrant?

510
00:32:46,714 --> 00:32:47,923
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

511
00:32:47,924 --> 00:32:49,008
A confession.

512
00:32:50,134 --> 00:32:52,511
We gotta force him to confess.
We can still do it.

513
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:54,389
It's him. I know it is.

514
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:56,641
Hold on, his garden.

515
00:32:58,601 --> 00:33:01,521
He asked his neighbor
to take care of his garden for two days.

516
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:05,900
Without a warrant, the most
we can hold him for is up to 48 hours.

517
00:33:07,193 --> 00:33:09,861
What's the law in Korea
if you're released after 48 hours

518
00:33:09,862 --> 00:33:11,823
cause the cops can't find any evidence?

519
00:33:21,624 --> 00:33:23,334
Without sufficient evidence...

520
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:29,590
you can't get a warrant
for the same charge.

521
00:33:30,091 --> 00:33:34,971
And that means that man is free.

522
00:33:44,647 --> 00:33:48,568
Copy that. Team Two, move out.
Team Two, move out!

523
00:33:55,158 --> 00:33:56,700
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.
- Hey, watch it!

524
00:33:56,701 --> 00:33:58,161
What happened?

525
00:33:58,786 --> 00:34:00,580
They just found a body, a new one.

526
00:34:01,080 --> 00:34:02,706
Which means we fucked up. Ah, man.

527
00:34:02,707 --> 00:34:04,167
Chief! Let's go!

528
00:34:50,004 --> 00:34:54,425
SHALL REMAIN HIDDEN

529
00:35:23,454 --> 00:35:25,455
ONE FEAR
GIVES BIRTH TO ENDLESS FEARS

530
00:35:25,456 --> 00:35:29,043
BUT ITS METHODS
SHALL REMAIN HIDDEN

531
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:05,370
Whoa, whoa. What are you doing?

532
00:36:05,371 --> 00:36:09,083
Hey, you can't just go in there!
Ah! What the hell?

533
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:13,337
- Yoo I-jin, an elementary school teacher.
- Hey!

534
00:36:13,838 --> 00:36:15,005
Get off! Please, get off of me!

535
00:36:15,006 --> 00:36:16,840
You just had to murder another?

536
00:36:16,841 --> 00:36:19,467
- Hey! Stop!
- Let me go!

537
00:36:19,468 --> 00:36:20,636
Get off him!

538
00:36:21,596 --> 00:36:24,181
Kim Seok! Take a breath!

539
00:36:24,182 --> 00:36:25,808
You're a cop, goddamn it!

540
00:36:28,644 --> 00:36:31,564
Uh... Oh.

541
00:36:33,399 --> 00:36:34,400
Kim Seok...

542
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:37,612
Huh.

543
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:41,157
Thank you for your hard work.

544
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,910
I appreciate it, Detective.

545
00:36:49,957 --> 00:36:53,376
Reports claim that the newest victim
was waiting to be rescued.

546
00:36:53,377 --> 00:36:57,005
Meanwhile, the suspect was subjected
to over 40 hours of interrogations,

547
00:36:57,006 --> 00:37:00,050
due to the fact that his vehicle
and house fit their descriptions.

548
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:02,427
There have been concerns
that the handling of this investigation

549
00:37:02,428 --> 00:37:06,265
could create tensions with Japan
just before the Korea-Japan World Cup...

550
00:37:08,351 --> 00:37:10,144
What can you say about the latest victim?

551
00:37:10,978 --> 00:37:13,105
Block them. Block those cameras.

552
00:37:17,693 --> 00:37:19,487
Don't you have anything
to say for yourself?

553
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:21,446
Sir, we just have a few questions!

554
00:37:21,447 --> 00:37:22,948
Would you like to make a statement?

555
00:37:22,949 --> 00:37:25,116
Do you feel any remorse at all?

556
00:37:25,117 --> 00:37:27,702
Sir, did they pressure you to confess?

557
00:37:27,703 --> 00:37:29,372
Just a few words, please!

558
00:37:35,211 --> 00:37:36,920
All right, everyone disperse!

559
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:38,839
I mean it, time to leave! Let's go!

560
00:37:39,966 --> 00:37:41,675
What's he doing? Get this, get this!

561
00:37:41,676 --> 00:37:42,760
I'm on it!

562
00:37:45,346 --> 00:37:46,639
I'm innocent!

563
00:37:48,849 --> 00:37:50,309
I didn't do it!

564
00:38:02,863 --> 00:38:04,490
Follow him! Hurry, in the car!

565
00:38:11,247 --> 00:38:15,126
Even if we had gotten the warrant in time,
he'd have never left anything in that car.

566
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:19,255
After he got rid of the body,
he made sure to get ahead of us.

567
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:22,132
That's why he came
on his own to the station.

568
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:23,425
It's why he asked for the time.

569
00:38:23,426 --> 00:38:28,723
He was most likely keeping track of when
someone would find her at the warehouse.

570
00:38:32,977 --> 00:38:33,978
If I'd...

571
00:38:36,856 --> 00:38:40,318
If I would have tracked
Emi Shunsuke's whereabouts first,

572
00:38:41,068 --> 00:38:43,362
instead of jumping
straight to arresting him...

573
00:38:45,031 --> 00:38:46,866
Or if I'd done a sweep of the area.

574
00:38:52,413 --> 00:38:53,789
Then I might have saved her.

575
00:38:55,207 --> 00:38:58,418
It happened over 30 kilometers from here.

576
00:38:58,419 --> 00:39:00,337
We looked everywhere
within our targeted radius.

577
00:39:00,338 --> 00:39:01,963
There is no way
we could have prevented it.

578
00:39:01,964 --> 00:39:03,466
I'm aware, that's why I said "if".

579
00:39:07,511 --> 00:39:08,888
Stop that.

580
00:39:09,638 --> 00:39:11,932
No "ifs" for us.

581
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:25,278
HEAD OF UNIT - THE GUY WE
QUESTIONED IS FILING A COMPLAINT.

582
00:39:25,279 --> 00:39:26,363
GET BACK HERE NOW.

583
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:28,866
Emi's gonna file a complaint against us
with the Seoul Police.

584
00:39:31,243 --> 00:39:32,244
Son of a...

585
00:39:33,579 --> 00:39:35,163
Well, isn't that lucky?

586
00:39:35,164 --> 00:39:36,248
Huh?

587
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:41,670
'Cause that then means,
he's leaving his house empty.

588
00:39:46,342 --> 00:39:48,177
You stay, I'll handle it.

589
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:50,762
Alone? In Korea?

590
00:39:50,763 --> 00:39:53,891
- Yeah.
- No way. Nice try.

591
00:39:56,018 --> 00:39:58,020
We promised her we'd catch him.

592
00:40:00,481 --> 00:40:01,816
Lee Hyeon-seo.

593
00:40:03,401 --> 00:40:04,402
We promised.

594
00:40:05,403 --> 00:40:06,695
We have to get him.

595
00:40:11,992 --> 00:40:14,495
Don't worry.
I'm here on assignment anyway.

596
00:40:19,417 --> 00:40:20,709
Promise you'll be careful.

597
00:40:39,270 --> 00:40:40,271
Huh.

598
00:40:48,028 --> 00:40:49,321
Uh-huh.

599
00:40:53,701 --> 00:40:55,536
I can jump that, no problem.

600
00:40:57,246 --> 00:40:59,790
Gotta get my bearings.

601
00:41:10,551 --> 00:41:13,554
Yeah, still got it.

602
00:41:18,350 --> 00:41:21,437
Doesn't look very Korean.
It's like we're still in Japan.

603
00:42:11,904 --> 00:42:12,905
Huh.

604
00:42:17,952 --> 00:42:18,953
Huh?
